# Workflow

## 1. Plan

3+ steps, new project, or architecture -> brief plan + scope confirm first.
See [confirm-system-before-build.mdc](confirm-system-before-build.mdc).

## 2. Route by trigger

**Never browse skill lists.** Match phrase -> trigger -> open one `SKILL.md`.

1. Extract triggers from request
2. Match in [SKILL-GRAPH.md](~/.cursor/skills/SKILL-GRAPH.md) (<=2 passes); [LLM.md](~/.cursor/skills/LLM.md) secondary
3. Open matched skill -> follow steps
4. **One skill/turn** (default)
   - SysML: checklist + workflow hubs + <=1 `sysml-*` specialist
   - Selector may return short `order[]` -- open those only, in order

Ids: seed.wire `@SKL` via SKILL-GRAPH.md. Constraints: [user-pack-skills-catalog.mdc](user-pack-skills-catalog.mdc).

## 3. Tiered handoff (store vs LLM feed)

| Pri | When | Format |
|-----|------|--------|
| 0 | In-prompt / author-facing (always) | English pins + short imperatives; write=display (`[Id] --(Rel)--> [Id] ; key=value`). Not raw `@TAG|pipe` dumps. |
| 1-2 | MemNet up / down | [memnet-goldfish-loop.mdc](memnet-goldfish-loop.mdc) (plain Markdown when down; no TOON/TRON) |
| 3 | MCP/CLI boundary | JSON only |

Store grammar: [memnet-format](~/.cursor/skills/memnet-format/SKILL.md). Hub: [AGENTS.md](~/.cursor/skills/AGENTS.md).

## 4. Execute lean

- MemNet loop on multi-step/SysML: [memnet-goldfish-loop.mdc](memnet-goldfish-loop.mdc)
- MCP before bulk file reads; lazy-load `references/` only when a step needs them

## 5. Verify / lessons

Proof = commands run + sane output. Corrections -> `tasks/lessons.md` (or repo equivalent).

